            "url": "https://x.com/x-user-16/status/2095988914813379040",
            "content": {
              "text": "ANTHROPIC JUST PUBLISHED A 10-MINUTE DEMO WHERE ONE PROMPT RAN FOR 90 MINUTES ALONE.\n\nIt shows Claude Code shipping a full table component into the Excalidraw repo from a single prompt, 90 minutes of unedited output, lint and tests passing before a human looks at it.\n\n1:22 → you move Claude Code from the terminal into your IDE\n4:42 → you approve each diff inline with the surrounding code\n5:21 → you hand off one prompt for 90 unattended minutes\n6:15 → you get a table you can resize, recolor and fill\n8:08 → many Claude Codes in parallel on flaky tests and triage\n8:25 → the docs commit lands in your PR untouched by you\n\nYou don't need to know the Excalidraw codebase or write a line of the feature yourself.\n\nThe real unlock isn't faster code, it's a teammate you delegate to across the terminal, the IDE and GitHub while you work on something else.\n\nSave it and watch it today.\n\nThen read \"How to Unlock the Full Potential of Fable 5.1\" below.",
