        {
          "post": {
            "id": "2095976334258536612",
            "url": "https://x.com/x-user-19/status/2095976334258536612",
            "content": {
              "text": "THE BEST AI CODING AGENT MAY BE THE ONE THAT WORKS ALL NIGHT AND STILL ISN’T ALLOWED TO MERGE.\n\nThis repo ops setup is basically a 24/7 engineering night shift.\n\nWhile you sleep, agents can:\n\nmonitor CI,\nclassify failures,\ncatch flaky tests,\nwatch dependencies for CVEs,\nwrite trivial patches,\nrun the test suite,\nand open draft PRs.\n\nKimi’s swarm can scale the monitoring across up to 300 sub-agents, while Grok handles the actual repo workflow.\n\nBut the most important part is the boundary.\n\nFlaky test? Fix it.\nLint failure? Fix it.\nApplication logic? Stop.\nSecurity-critical change? Escalate.\nMerge to production? Human only.\n\nI think that’s a much more useful definition of autonomous coding.\n\nNot:\n\n“AI can change anything while I sleep.”\n\nBut:\n\n“AI can make sure I never wake up to something that could’ve been safely handled without me.”\n\nThe goal isn’t removing the engineer.\n\nIt’s removing the 2AM version of the engineer.",
