          "post": {
            "id": "2095950629315195174",
            "url": "https://x.com/x-user-25/status/2095950629315195174",
            "content": {
              "text": "One person can realistically watch 2-3 repos by hand before something breaks loudly enough to notice. A Kimi K3 swarm just watched 300 sub-agents across the same setup, and the part that should actually change how you think about repo maintenance isn't the number, it's what got automated versus what deliberately didn't.\n\nHere's the boundary that makes this actually safe instead of reckless: the fix-engine only touches flaky tests, lint, and formatting, full stop. Anything that looks like real application logic gets routed straight to a human, on purpose, because a model confidently patching an actual bug wrong is worse than that bug sitting untriaged for a day. Fix Bot opens pull requests. It never merges them. That's not a limitation waiting to be lifted later, it's the one rule the entire desk is built around.\n\nThe genuinely clever part is how the two tools split the job. Grok Bot is the cockpit, six named bots you brief in plain English, Triage, Fix, Test, Dependency, Release, Alert, each with its own narrow lane. Kimi K3 is the engine underneath doing the actual load-bearing work nobody sees, holding a repo's full file tree and git history in one million-token context without chunking, so it reasons over what actually happened instead of a lossy summary that lost the detail that mattered.\n\nThe real test isn't whether the automation runs, it's whether it earns trust one repo at a time. Point the whole stack at your lowest-stakes repo first and watch the patch acceptance rate. If Fix Bot's pull requests get merged without edits most of the time, add a second repo. If they keep getting closed and rewritten, you tighten the scope before you scale anything further, not after.\n\nThis doesn't replace judgment, it replaces the version of you that used to check CI at 2am because nobody else was going to. What's still eating your 2am right now that has a scope narrow enough to hand off?",
              "media_urls": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2095928946516758532/img/Mf5V6hLmbHOXPZga.jpg",
              "thumbnail_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2095928946516758532/img/Mf5V6hLmbHOXPZga.jpg",
              "duration_seconds": 787.513
